@startuml
title Master Odometry - Typical Usage Flow (e.g., OdometryLong)

|Application|
start
:Create `modom::cOdometry` instance;
:Create `OdometryLong` provider instance\n(pass `cOdometry` pointer);
:Use `OdometryControl` to configure\nglobal and provider parameters;

|Data Input Thread|
while (Receiving data from CAN/Sensor?) is (yes)
  :Receive raw sensor data;
  :Fill `strCarOdom_t` sample struct;
  :Calculate CRC for the sample;
  :Call `odomLongProvider.addSample(sample)`;
  |Odometry Library|
  :Perform validity checks (CRC, timestamp, etc.);
  if (Sample is valid and new?) then (yes)
    :Store sample in internal\ncircular buffer `m_carOdomProcBufs`;
  else (no)
    :Discard sample;
  endif
|Data Input Thread|
endwhile

|Application Thread|
while (Need Odometry Data?) is (yes)
  :Get `request_ts_us` (e.g., from camera frame);
  :Call `odomLongProvider.getOdometry(output, request_ts_us)`;
  |Odometry Library|
  switch (Processing Mode?)
  case ( ODOM_PRC_INT_LONG_WR )
    :Call `getSignals(interpolated_sample, request_ts_us)`;
    partition "Signal Interpolation" {
      :Collect relevant samples from buffer\naround `request_ts_us`;
      :Use `OdometryInterp` (and `SampleExtrapolator`)\nto perform weighted regression;
      :Fill `interpolated_sample` with results;
    }
    :Call `populateIn(interpolated_sample)`;
    :Fill `modom::ODM_in` struct;
    :Call `m_modom->addSignals(...)`;
    :Fallthrough to mOdom update;
  case ( ODOM_PRC_INT_LONG_ALL )
    :Iterate through all new samples in buffer;
    :Call `populateIn(sample)` for each;
    :Fill `modom::ODM_in` struct;
    :Call `m_modom->addSignals(...)`;
    :Fallthrough to mOdom update;
  case ( other modes )
    :Select/interpolate sample based on mode;
    :Call `populateIn(selected_sample)`;
    :Fallthrough to mOdom update;
  endswitch
  partition "mOdom Core Calculation" {
    :Call `m_modom->update(request_ts_us, output)`;
    :mOdom performs internal calculations\nand populates the `modom::ODM_out` struct;
  }
  :Return `true` and the `output` data;
|Application Thread|
  :Use the `modom::ODM_out` data;
endwhile

stop
@enduml
